{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Remove the 20% VAT on all veterinary medical treatments and diagnostic tests",
        "additional_details": "Currently, human medical care is exempt from VAT but veterinary care attracts 20% VAT. We think this creates an unfair financial penalty on regular families trying to keep their animals healthy.\r\n \r\nWhile many commercial farms and other VAT-registered businesses can reclaim VAT on veterinary costs, most pet owners and many animal welfare charities cannot reclaim this VAT.\r\n \r\nWe believe that paying a 20% tax on life-saving surgeries, diagnostics, and medications essentially treats animal healthcare as a luxury consumer service and the Government should stop it.",
        "background": "We want the Government to exempt, or apply a zero rate of VAT to, veterinary medical treatments, surgeries, medicines and diagnostic tests. We believe veterinary care is an essential medical necessity, not a luxury commercial service, and should not be taxed as an unavoidable consumer expense.",
